      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find the range of the function $f(x)=-2(x-1)^{2}-8.$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$f(x)\\le $\n{{field-3}}",
      "worked_solution": "The parabola is written in vertex form, \n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the leading coefficient and $(h,k)$ is the vertex. \n\n- Since $h=1$ and $k=-8,$ the vertex is $(1,-8).$\n\n- Since $a=-2<0,$ the parabola opens downwards.\n\nBecause the parabola opens downwards, there is no minimum output, and the vertex corresponds to the maximum output.\n\nTherefore, the range is $(-\\infty ,-8],$ i.e. $-\\infty <f(x)\\le -8.$\n\nThe corresponding diagram is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14269734/assets/b641825e1b39599dba76238fc9dd636e038617413e732eff6d8b470fa9c316c4.png)",
